    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Step 10: Run a plain regression model (the spline setup, but with no penalty added) and measured how well it generalizes using cross-validation. Tested it on 5 different slices of the training data and averaging the error. Then trained it one final time on the entire training set so there's an actual usable model saved, not just a score. Result: about $34,500 average error per home. Ran the top 5 results to establish the correct alpha. Set up a range of called alphas to test for Ridge regression, starting narrow (0.001 to 1,000), then widening it out to 100,000 to double check that the best value found wasn't just sitting at the edge of the first range tried."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SAbRZtDRSXPV"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Build the unregularized spline-regression baseline.\n",
        "pipeline_lr = build_spline_model(\n",
        "    LinearRegression()\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Estimate generalization performance using training-data cross-validation.\n",
        "lr_cv_rmse_scores = -cross_val_score(\n",
        "    pipeline_lr,\n",
        "    X_train,\n",
        "    y_train,\n",
        "    scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
        "    cv=CV,\n",
        "    n_jobs=-1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fit the baseline to the complete training set after cross-validation.\n",
        "pipeline_lr.fit(\n",
        "    X_train,\n",
        "    y_train\n",
        ")\n",
